  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 941292,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "The report describes a critical heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the libvips image processing library used by Basecamp. The analysis found that a mismatch between the TIFF container component count (1 byte/pixel) and the embedded JPEG output (2 bytes/pixel) leads to a deterministic heap buffer overwrite. The researcher provided clear reproduction steps, multiple proof-of-concept files, and demonstrated the potential for remote code execution through control-flow hijacking.",
